# Line endings.
#
# Prettier is configured `endOfLine: "lf"`, and `npm run format:check` is a
# blocking CI step. Without this file the answer depends on the platform:
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the Windows default, so a fresh clone there gets a
# CRLF working tree, prettier rejects every file, and the same command that
# passes on the Linux runner fails locally.
#
# Forcing LF in the working tree everywhere makes the check platform
# independent. The repository already stores LF, so this changes checkout
# behaviour rather than content. After pulling this, an existing clone may
# need `git add --renormalize .` once.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never convert, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.node binary
*.riv binary
